{
  "name": "Triage Gmail with Gemini: label every email, draft replies, log invoices to Sheets and get urgent alerts on Telegram",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "12172647-03df-467f-9848-32233deab320",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -830,
        -121
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 852,
        "content": "## Triage Gmail with Gemini: label every email, draft replies, log invoices to Sheets and get urgent alerts on Telegram\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow watches Gmail for new messages, loads configurable user settings, reads the email, and asks Gemini to classify it. Based on Gemini\u2019s structured result, it applies or creates Gmail labels, leaves draft replies when needed, logs invoice details to Google Sheets, sends urgent alerts to Telegram, and records each triage decision in an n8n data table.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect Gmail credentials for the trigger, reading emails, listing/creating labels, applying labels, and creating drafts.\n- Connect Google Gemini credentials and confirm the primary and backup classification prompts/models are configured.\n- Create or select the Google Sheets spreadsheet for invoice logging, then set the correct invoices_sheet_id in the **Set Email Parameters** node. Its first row must have: Date, Issuer, Number, Net, VAT, Total, Currency, Subject, Link to the email.\n- Connect Telegram bot credentials and configure the chat or recipient used by the alert node.\n- Review the **Set Email Parameters** node values for your_name, business, tone, and any other workflow-specific defaults before activating the workflow. Leave `telegram_chat_id` empty to skip alerts; set `create_drafts` to false for labels only.\n- Nothing is ever sent for you: replies stay as drafts, and anything Gemini does not know stays in [brackets].\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the Gemini classification prompt, label mapping, reply tone, invoice row fields, and urgency criteria to match your mailbox and business process.\n\nMade by **Amelqa** \u00b7 amelqa.com"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
